Subject: Cantor Recursive Machine Schema Semantic Refinement

@ [refinement_uuid] f63b8c56-2337-4688-a72c-55f4b1b6ee05

& [Terms] are disambiguated
  + schema_document_depth is maximum nesting of the JSON Schema document itself
  + definition_graph_depth is longest acyclic path after treating revisited definitions as terminal references
  + instance_container_depth is nested JSON object and array depth before typed decode
  + semantic_value_depth is recursive ProcedureType or ProcedureValue depth checked by Cantor
  + local_recursive_reference is a fragment-only reference into the same canonical document or bundle
  + cycle_guard is visited identity plus active traversal stack preventing recursive generator expansion
  + recursive_residual is a non-schema rule that remains enforced by parser or Cantor validation

& [RefinedMeaning] is finite graph not finite unrolling
  + canonical bytes contain each named definition once
  + recursion is represented by stable local references
  + graph traversal counts each definition once and detects self or mutual cycles without following them indefinitely
  + instance depth is bounded independently before or during decode and again by Cantor semantic validation

& [Honesty] rejects false equivalence
  + JSON Schema recursive acceptance does not prove maximum_call_depth
  + serde depth rejection may be stricter than semantic depth because enclosing transport objects also consume container depth
  + conformance agreement is claimed only for syntax rules expressible and enabled in both readers
  + depth behavior is tested and residualized rather than hidden

